WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.440
Welcome to Incident Resolution and Prevention. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Restore service and prevent recurring operational incidents.

2
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:20.270
Consider this scenario. The same production incident reappears each Friday. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:30.370
Start with two steps: Log and prioritize incidents. Then Restore service within agreed needs. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:39.880
Continue with Analyze patterns and causes. Then Verify prevention effectiveness. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:39.880 --> 00:01:00.340
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous incident log, service recovery record, repeat-incident trend tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: closing tickets without addressing systemic recurrence; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:14.590
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
